  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As we know that,\r\nImpulse, $I=$ force $(F) \\times$ small time interval\r\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\r\nI=m a \\times t & {[\\because F=m a]} \\\\\r\nI=[\\mathrm{M}]\\left[\\mathrm{LT}^{-2}\\right] \\times[\\mathrm{T}] \\\\\r\nI=\\left[\\mathrm{MLT}^{-1}\\right]\r\n\\end{array}$\r\nHence, the correct dimensional formula for impulse is given by $\\left[\\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{L} \\mathrm{T}^{-1} 1 .\\right.$",
